     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>I would use a global variable. Note the use of &quot;&lt;&lt;-&quot; to assign a &quot;value&quot; to the global variable.<br><br><code><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><code><code><span style=\"color:#000\">sliceBox</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> &lt;- list()</span></code></code><br><br>server </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br></span><span style=\"color:#000\">  ...<br><br>  rootNode </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> newNode</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div></code></div>"
    ],
